## Quick Reference

### Common Tasks
```bash
# Start development environment
make docker-up && make db-init && make run

# Run tests
make test

# Check code quality
go fmt ./... && go vet ./... && make test

# Update documentation
./scripts/utils/check-doc-sync.sh

# Full development cycle
make test-full && go fmt ./... && ./scripts/utils/check-doc-sync.sh
```

### Git Commit Format
```
<type>(<scope>): <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer]
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`

---

## Remember

- **Test First**: Write tests before or alongside code
- **Document Always**: Update docs with every change
- **Incremental**: Small, focused changes with tests
- **Quality**: Format, lint, and test before committing
- **Consistency**: Follow project conventions and patterns
